{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-frobenius-relation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:frobenius-relation","kind":"proposition","title":"Frobenius relation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-frobenius-pairing"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-frobenius-relation"],"examples":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-frobenius-su2","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-frobenius-relation-su2"],"tags":["category-theory","frobenius"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.frobenius_relation","text":"frobenius-relation.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-relation.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:frobenius-relation\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a <a href=\"#def:quantum-universe\">quantum universe</a>. Denote by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Delta_\\mu</code> the comultiplication on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> dual to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mu</code> under the <a href=\"#def:frobenius-pairing\">Frobenius pairing</a>. This compatibility makes <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> a Frobenius algebra. The <em>Frobenius relation</em> holds:</p>\n<figure class=\"tex-svg\"><img data-src=\"rendered/quantum-universes/frobenius-relation-0.svg\" alt=\"\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:frobenius-relation}\n\\begin{gathered}\n\\begin{tikzcd}[row sep=2.5em, column sep=3.5em]\n  A \\otimes A\n    \\ar[r, &quot;\\mathrm{id} \\otimes \\Delta_\\mu&quot;]\n    \\ar[d, &quot;\\mu&quot;']\n  &amp; A \\otimes A \\otimes A\n    \\ar[d, &quot;\\mu \\otimes \\mathrm{id}&quot;]\n  \\\\\n  A \\ar[r, &quot;\\Delta_\\mu&quot;']\n  &amp; A \\otimes A\n\\end{tikzcd}\n\\\\[-0.5em]\n\\text{\\small Frobenius relation: } (\\mu \\otimes \\mathrm{id}) \\circ (\\mathrm{id} \\otimes \\Delta_\\mu) = \\Delta_\\mu \\circ \\mu\n\\end{gathered}\n\\end{equation}\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>\n<p>Sliding a multiplication past a comultiplication yields the same result as composing them.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/frobenius-relation.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Proposition","number":"2.5.1"}
